How to Practice PLCs for Free
Option 1: PLC Simulator Software

Start immediately with:

PLC Fiddle
Browser-based.
Free ladder logic simulator.
No installation.

Good for:

Timers
Counters
Interlocks
Motor control logic
Factory I/O
3D factory simulation.
Widely used for learning.
Works with multiple PLC platforms.

You can simulate:

Conveyors
Sensors
Packaging machines
Traffic systems

This is one of the best tools available.

Option 2: Siemens TIA Portal Simulation

Install:

TIA Portal
PLCSIM

You can create:

Start/Stop circuits
Conveyor systems
Sorting machines
Alarm systems

without owning a PLC.

Option 3: Use an ESP32 as the Physical Process

You already work with ESP32.

Build:

Pushbuttons
Relays
LEDs
Sensors

Then have the PLC simulator control the process logic.

This teaches:

Inputs
Outputs
Sequencing
State machines

which is exactly what you'll do in industry.

